dua-core: route Mac OS X on powerpc to the portable std::fs walker. The macOS backend (src/macos) enumerates
directories with getattrlistbulk(2), which only exists from OS X 10.10 (xnu-2782); the 10.5/10.6 SDKs have no
such symbol, so every binary linking dua-core fails with `Undefined symbols: _getattrlistbulk, referenced from
dua_core::macos::ReadDir::refill` (gitoxide 0.61.0 `ein`/`gix` through gitoxide-core's organize feature, which
only runs `Options::skip_metadata()` walks). The non-Windows, non-macOS backend uses only std::fs (read_dir +
symlink_metadata) and works on 10.5 and 10.6: every `target_os = "macos"` cfg in lib.rs now also requires a
non-powerpc arch. The `[target.'cfg(target_os = "macos")'.dependencies] libc` entry stays (unused on powerpc).
`Options::apfs_clone_metadata` (and its Default initialiser) keeps plain `target_os = "macos"` so callers keep
compiling; the portable walker ignores it (no APFS before 10.13).
Base: dua-core 4.1.0; checked to apply to 4.2.0 and 5.0.0 (latest on 2026-10-25).

